# The compiled French catalogue is committed, and it is a binary file with a
# length-prefixed string table. Git guesses binary correctly today, but a wrong
# guess would rewrite line endings inside it and the app would silently fall
# back to English — so say it outright.
*.mo binary

# Anything the Linux container executes must keep LF endings, whatever the
# machine that checked it out prefers. A shell script with CRLF fails with
# "no such file or directory" pointing at the interpreter — the shebang line
# ends in a carriage return, so the kernel looks for `/bin/sh\r` — which is
# among the least informative error messages in circulation.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
deploy/entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
